<ContentLayout
  title="Watch Multiple YouTube Live Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Watch multiple YouTube live streams and chats at once. Learn which URLs work, how live chat behaves, and how to troubleshoot embedded videos."
  heading="Watch multiple YouTube live streams at once"
  platform="youtube"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix arranges multiple YouTube live broadcasts in one browser
    workspace. Keep an official event feed beside alternate camera angles,
    creator commentary, or several live chats, then resize each window around
    the perspectives that matter most.
  </p>

  <h2>How to add multiple YouTube live streams</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the watch page for the live stream you want to add.</li>
    <li>
      Copy its URL, such as
      <code>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Paste the URL into the Stream Mix header. YouTube is selected
      automatically and the video ID is extracted.
    </li>
    <li>Choose Stream + Chat, Stream, or Chat and select Add.</li>
    <li>Repeat for the other broadcasts, then drag and resize the windows.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Stream Mix recognizes standard <code>youtube.com/watch?v=</code> links, shortened
    <code>youtu.be/</code> links, and YouTube <code>/live/</code> or
    <code>/embed/</code> URLs. You can also select YouTube manually and enter the
    video ID directly. A channel homepage is not enough because each YouTube broadcast
    has its own video ID.
  </p>

  <h2>Choose video, chat, or both</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stream + Chat</strong> places the embedded player and live chat side
      by side in one resizable window.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stream</strong> gives the video the full window and is the best choice
      for small secondary feeds.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Chat</strong> shows only the conversation for that video, which can
      be useful beside one large primary broadcast.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    YouTube players remain independent: play, pause, quality, captions, volume,
    and fullscreen are controlled inside each embed. Stream Mix does not
    synchronize broadcasts, and live feeds may naturally be several seconds
    apart because their creators and YouTube delivery settings differ.
  </p>

  <h2>When YouTube live chat is available</h2>
  <p>
    The Chat and Stream + Chat modes are intended for a currently live broadcast
    or Premiere whose creator has enabled live chat. Chat is disabled for
    made-for-kids content, and a creator can turn it off for any stream.
    Scheduled broadcasts that have not started and videos without an active
    embeddable chat may show an unavailable message.
  </p>

  <p>
    YouTube requires the chat embed to include the domain of the page displaying
    it. Stream Mix supplies that value automatically for both
    <code>streammix.app</code> and local development. YouTube also states that embedded
    live chat is not available on mobile web, so the chat-focused workspace is best
    used in a desktop browser. Read YouTube’s
    <a href="https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/2524549" rel="external"
      >official live chat instructions</a
    >
    for the platform rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Troubleshoot a YouTube stream or chat</h2>
  <h3>The URL adds the wrong item or is not accepted</h3>
  <p>
    Use the URL of the individual video rather than a channel or search page. In
    a standard watch URL, copy the value after <code>v=</code> if you want to enter
    the ID manually.
  </p>

  <h3>The player says the video is unavailable</h3>
  <p>
    First open the same video directly on YouTube. The broadcast may have ended,
    be private, have a regional or age restriction, or have embedding disabled
    by its owner. Those restrictions are enforced by YouTube and cannot be
    bypassed by Stream Mix.
  </p>

  <h3>Video works but live chat does not</h3>
  <p>
    Confirm that the broadcast is live and that chat appears on its YouTube
    watch page. If it does, check browser tracking protection and
    content-blocking extensions. Chat may also require signing in to YouTube
    before you can send messages.
  </p>

  <h3>Playback becomes slow with several videos</h3>
  <p>
    Multiple high-resolution players can use substantial CPU, memory, and
    bandwidth. Lower the quality of secondary feeds, pause video windows you are
    not watching, switch some panels to Chat only, or minimize them to the
    bottom shelf.
  </p>

  <h2>Mix YouTube with Twitch and Kick</h2>
  <p>
    You are not limited to one platform. Add
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-twitch-streams">Twitch channels</a> and
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-kick-streams">Kick channels</a> to the same layout,
    or follow the complete
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-streams">multistream viewing guide</a> to learn
    about sharing and Compact mode. The <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> covers saved layouts,
    privacy, and common embed behavior.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Open the YouTube multistream viewer</a>
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
